This directory must EXIST before the gateway container starts, and that
is the whole reason this file is here.

The tenant logos (RFC-0042 T3) are mounted in from the host at
/etc/caddy/static/place -- inside /etc/caddy/static, which is itself a
READ-ONLY bind mount. Docker creates a missing mountpoint before
mounting, and it cannot create one inside a read-only mount: the
gateway then refuses to start at all.

Found the hard way on oaap-test, 2026-09-23: the update rebuilt both
services, recreated the gateway, and the gateway did not come back --
  make mountpoint "/etc/caddy/static/place": read-only file system
Every HTTP route on the node was down until the directory existed.

So it exists here, it is copied to $APP_DIR/static/place by update.sh
like every other platform file, and Docker finds a mountpoint instead
of trying to make one.
